<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 2078 0 R
  /Alt (This conceptual illustration depicts a square area divided into three distinct land cover / land use (LULC) classes. The top-right portion, shaded dark green, is labelled 'Woody'. The central, light green band is labelled 'Permanent herbaceous'. The bottom-left area, coloured blue, is labelled 'Water'. This visual representation demonstrates the adjacency of these different land cover types within a single conceptual unit or pixel, aligning with class definitions for the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) CLC+ Backbone Raster Product. 'Woody' corresponds to CLMS class 5 (Low-growing woody plants), 'Permanent herbaceous' to class 6, and 'Water' to class 10.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 2547 0 R
>>
